From: ReArc Authors
Subject: [PATCH] P-TAB-001 process details for the host's task manager (ABI 1.65)

The host's Task Manager window (Chrome's Window > Task manager) could list
the engine's processes from ReArcEngineGetProcesses but could not name them
as Chrome does or fill the Network column: the list says which tabs have a
frame in a renderer, not which of them have their page there, names an
extension's process only as "an extension", cannot tell the spare renderer
from any other renderer without a page, and counts no network bytes.

ReArcEngineGetProcessDetails returns the same rows and details_json, a JSON
object keyed by pid: main_frame_tabs and subframe_tabs (Chrome's "Tab:" and
"Subframe:" rows; frames of a page kept for Back or loading ahead are in
neither), site (the subframes' site URL), extension_id and extension_name
(ProcessMap::GetEnabledExtensionByProcessID), spare
(SpareRenderProcessHostManager::GetSpares), title (ChildProcessData::name,
"Network Service") and network_bytes. JSON, so a host can call it by symbol
lookup without the new header and later keys need no struct change.

network_bytes counts the network service's data-use reports, the same ones
Chrome's task manager counts: ChromeContentBrowserClient::
OnNetworkServiceDataUseUpdate also calls rearc::perf::RecordNetworkBytes,
per RenderProcessHost, and what no frame asked for goes to the browser as
TaskManagerImpl::UpdateAccumulatedStatsNetworkForRoute does. The reports are
off by default (NetworkService::EnableDataUseUpdates). Each details request
switches them on (again, so a restarted network service keeps reporting),
and the first report that arrives more than 5 s after the last request
switches them off: nothing is counted and no timer runs while the host's
window is closed.

ReArcEngineGetProcesses is unchanged for a host: its collector moved into
CollectProcesses, shared by both calls. No call is added for End task: the
processes are the host's own children, Chrome's task manager on macOS
signals them as well (Task::Kill, base::Process::Terminate, SIGTERM), and a
tab whose renderer was killed already reports is_crashed
(WebContentsImpl::IsCrashed counts TERMINATION_STATUS_PROCESS_WAS_KILLED).

Built into the release engine (overlay adbb86cb3f, out/ReArc-codecs-arm64)
and shipped in 2026.1117.849; its self-test step (task manager) passes and
the Task Manager window showed live network figures on screen.
engine/tests/c_abi_perf_host.mm has the new step and has not run.

Bridge 0.75.0, ABI 1.65, feature task_manager. No struct changes.

Last rebased: 2026-11-17 onto Chromium 156.0.8078.100 (overlay 2f23d016ce).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5.2 <noreply@anthropic.com>

